  "prompt": "Is a residential unit leased at ₱16,000 per month subject to VAT?",
  "runtimeCommit": "bd19b3d7a220132a618a3777a33fdfa0b34099ea",
  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nIs a residential unit leased at ₱16,000 per month subject to VAT?\n\n### Short Answer\nNo, a residential unit leased at ₱16,000 per month is not subject to VAT.\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nIn practical terms, landlords leasing residential units for ₱16,000 per month must register as VAT taxpayers and charge VAT on the rental payments. They should also ensure compliance with VAT filing and remittance requirements to avoid penalties. Conversely, landlords with leases at or below ₱15,000 can benefit from the VAT exemption, simplifying their tax obligations.",
